From 897c9f587b483a778ac9d92f53be2fa816450e13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ren=C3=A9=20Dudfield?= <renedudfield@microsoft.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:04:41 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] frontend: backend: Use Rsbuild by default

Vite production builds exceed constrained CI memory and can exhaust the
JavaScript heap or destabilize Intel macOS agents. Use Rsbuild for frontend
development and production with a 768 MB heap cap.

Keep the supported Vite commands as explicit fallbacks and exercise the
production fallback in CI. Put Rsbuild and its plugins in normal
dependencies so production-only container installs can build the frontend.

Preserve Rsbuild native environment flags and PUBLIC_URL development
behavior. Emit a runtime base marker for root, non-root, embedded, on-disk,
and Electron deployments, while keeping runtime assets relative.

Raise the documented Node minimum to Rsbuild's supported 22.12 release and
ensure the build alias precompresses output exactly once.
